ABOUT ELEMENTS Elements is the quickest place for property and real estate professionals to outsource their marketing. We edit photos, convert sketches into floorplans and create video slideshows - all from client files uploaded via our easy-to-use portal. The Elements mission is to empower people with the tools, expertise and help needed to sell and let property better, faster and with more wow factor. As of 2023, we've processed 150,000+ orders for 1000+ clients across the globe. We are about to embark on a major project where we are pivoting away from overseas manual labour processing the orders to AI and machine learning processing the orders. From July 2023 we’ll begin training a series of AI models using our vast library of images - this new project is called Pixflair. THE PIXFLAIR PROJECT Pixflair will be an AI-powered image enhancement platform for maximising the visual appeal of property photos. Pixflair automates the editing process so real estate professionals can quickly and easily get visually stunning sets of images that maximise the appeal of homes coming to market without the need for any photo-editing skills. Users log in to their account via a browser to upload their photos. Our specially trained AI then automatically and instantly performs a suite of 20 useful photo edits including adding blue sky, boosting colours, straightening walls, and removing unwanted objects like cars, bins or clutter. It's all done on an easy-to-use SaaS platform that offers the power of Photoshop with the simplicity of drag-and-drop. Users can download the edited photos a few seconds later. A later phase of the project will see the Pixflair product be made available to larger B2B clients via an API. WHERE YOU'LL FIT You'll be a vital part of the team to bring to life the new Pixflair client portal that will help skyrocket the growth of the company and help in our transition to becoming a SaaS business. We're a small but mighty bunch! Alex (our founder) is also the Product Manager and UI Designer, he will provide the designs in Figma and advise on how the system must work. Adam is our Senior Engineering Consultant, he advises on high-level infrastructure and system architecture (amongst other things). He has already helped us define our Software Requirements and an Entity Relationship Diagram. Kieran is our Data Science expert who will train the AI models to edit real estate photos from our large data set of images. WHAT YOU'LL DO You will be the main engineer responsible for developing the front end and back end of the new client portal. Working remotely but alongside our engineering team, you will… - Work collaboratively with Alex, Adam and Kieran to ensure that all aspects of the project are delivered as planned. - Work through our System Requirements to build out the front end and back end of the new client portal to facilitate the uploading and downloading of real estate images. - Integrate the new client portal with the AI models that will edit the photos. - Focus on quality, ensuring that deliverables are complete, deployable, and accompanied by all appropriate documentation and supporting functionality. - Deliver clean and structured code which is well-tested and consistently error free. - Ensure the portal is scalable and secure. - Troubleshoot and debug issues as they arise. - Stay up-to-date with the latest web development trends and technologies. WHAT YOU'LL BRING TO THE ROLE ## Minimum requirements - Experience in building complex web applications - Experience with front-end technologies including React and Typescript - Experience with back-end technologies including nodeJS, NestJS framework, Typescript, OpenAPI, Auth0 - Experience with MySQL databases - Experience working with AWS services including S3 and SQS - Experience working with the Stripe API to facilitate payments - Understanding of RESTful web services and API development - Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail - Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment - Excellent communication skills - Comfortable working autonomously ## Desirables - Experience using things like Chat or Github CoPilot to help code faster - Experience with Figma integrations to quickly bring designs to life - Experience working in an AGILE framework in bi-weekly design sprints - An interest in real estate - An interest in photography We look forward to hearing from you :)
