We're seeking a talented full stack software engineer to help us modify an existing chatbot that utilizes ChatGPT and add two new features. The ideal candidate will have experience in Next.js, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, relational databases (Postgres), and vector search. The project is divided into several milestones, and we're open to working with an expert in Milestone 3. The successful candidate will work independently and may have the opportunity for more work in the future. The Chatbot is in a completed and functional state, but we're seeking to add a couple of features to modify it for a specific use case. Scope of work: Project Overview and Estimate 1. Chatbot UI Modification 2. Reference Document Integration 3. Vector Search Implementation 4. Beta Usage Site Preparation Details: - Independent work with potential for collaboration - Experience required: 5+ years - Opportunity for ongoing work as site is spun up and new features added. Maintenance of site would also be included in ongoing duties. Milestones: Before Work Begins: Project Overview and Estimate - Review current UI, documentation, and wireframe - Provide a detailed project estimate including time required for each milestone 1. Chatbot UI Modification - Modify existing chatbot and add some minor front-end changes - Apply color differentiation between user and chatbot text for better readability - Add a logo and buttons to one new feature and one existing feature 2. Reference Document Integration -Create a dedicated section for creating and managing reference documents - Allow AI to summarize and format reference materials based on user/admin preferences 3. Vector Search Implementation (if you have experience in this you are a top candidate) - Design and implement a vector search feature (expert assistance may be sought) - Optimize search functionality for accurate and contextually relevant results during prompting - Use of Supabase (preferred) for vector search (we can provide documentation), but open to other options such as Pinecone or Weaviate depending on if they can meet the functionality requirements. 4. Beta Usage Site Preparation - Test all implemented features and address any issues found - Set up a beta usage site for a limited number of users to collect feedback To apply, please submit your resume, a brief introduction explaining your experience with similar projects, and a link to your GitHub profile or other relevant work samples. We're excited to review your application and get this project going! Don't worry about getting the application perfect. Freelancers can send questions in their proposals, and we can connect later to discuss details.
